 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Esto, eso, aquello",
    "@en": "This, that, that"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "El coreano tiene tres distancias, como el español. **이** (este): cerca de mí. **그** (ese): cerca de ti. **저** (aquel): lejos de los dos.",
     "@en": "The Korean has three distances, like the Spanish. **이** (this): near me. **그** (that): near you. **저** (that one): away from both."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Delante de un nombre: **이 책** (este libro), **그 책** (ese libro), **저 책** (aquel libro).",
     "@en": "Before a name: **이 책** (this book), **그 책** (that book), **저 책** (that book)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Solos, al hablar: **이거** (esto), **그거** (eso), **저거** (aquello).",
     "@en": "Alone, when speaking: **이거** (this), **그거** (that), **저거** (that)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Cuando son el sujeto de la frase se acortan: **이게**, **그게**, **저게**. Por eso «¿qué es esto?» es **이게 뭐예요?**",
     "@en": "When they are the subject of the phrase they are shortened: **이게**, **그게**, **저게**. So «What is this?» is **이게 뭐예요?**"
    }
   ]
  },
